WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.710
So nice to see you again.

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.720
It's great to see you too.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.553
Yeah.

00:00:04.553 --> 00:00:07.050
I want to say this out
loud, your hair looks cute.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.190
You think it's cute? You like it.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.548
It's adorable.

00:00:10.548 --> 00:00:12.210
Thank you.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.540
It's really.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.920
That side flip. You can do that flip.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:16.753
There you go.

00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:18.390
And I can swoon,

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.980
What I want to do is keep growing it

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.610
till it's like down to here.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.480
And I want to do that thing.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.580
That would be so much fun.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.795
Make sure you invite me
back on when that happens.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.850
(laughing)

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.190
I see women do it in
reality shows all the time,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.565
they do this.

00:00:36.565 --> 00:00:38.062
Yes.

00:00:38.062 --> 00:00:40.140
Yeah, you want to be able to do that?

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.280
You're getting close.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.640
I'm getting there.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.320
First of all, you look
fantastic as you always do.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.750
And I'm curious,

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.990
first question I ask everybody these days

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.053
is how are you guys holding
up during the pandemic?

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.188
What's the Obama routine?

00:00:58.188 --> 00:01:00.020
What is you as a family,

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.230
'cause I know you're
all holed up together.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.550
What do you do?

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.480
Well, we've kind of had phases of COVID.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.200
There was sort of the early stages

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.668
where we were all excited to be together

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:12.100
and we were being all organized,

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.750
and we would spend the days
apart doing our respective work.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.980
The girls were still in
classes in the spring.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:23.070
And so we would be working and
then doing a little exercise,

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.060
then come together in the evenings

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.560
and we would have these activities.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.900
We'd have cocktails.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.080
And then we would work puzzles

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.020
and play games,

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.700
Barack taught the girls
how to play spades.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.603
Oh, really?

00:01:36.603 --> 00:01:37.436
Good.

00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:38.740
We actually had some organized things,

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.620
like we had an art exhibit day

00:01:42.319 --> 00:01:45.580
where we all went off and
did like watercolor paintings

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.370
and then we showed it.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.330
Now kind of this was in the early stages.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.193
Yes, I'm familiar.

00:01:53.658 --> 00:01:54.600
There was a period,

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.650
I know that we are going to say,

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.350
there was a period of
about a month or two,

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.340
maybe two and a half months,

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.650
of isn't this a rare
opportunity for all of us

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.040
to enjoy each other's company as a family.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.780
Then that went away.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.780
That went away, and it started,

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.673
I think first our kids
got a little sick of us.

00:02:13.254 --> 00:02:16.120
Which was fine, 'cause we
were pretty much sick of them.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.340
And so the summer started happening

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.030
and then we could be
outside a little bit more.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.160
And we came to the
vineyard where we still are

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.310
and so they have more room to roam around.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.580
[Conan] Yeah.
(indistinct)

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.640
that was good because it
helped us break it up.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:35.380
And now the kids are back
in Zoom land with classes,

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:39.070
they're doing it remotely and
they are no longer thrilled

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.330
about being with us.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.500
No, no.
So (static audio) periodically

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.993
for grunt.

00:02:43.993 --> 00:02:45.950
(laughing)

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.158
How about you and your husband?

00:02:49.158 --> 00:02:53.320
Are there moments where
you're thinking we all...

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.620
We tend to put figures like
yourselves and your husband

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.760
up on a pedestal and we forget

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.680
that you too can have
moments of Oh, it's that guy.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.620
Oh yeah. Oh yeah.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.297
We've talked about this.

00:03:05.297 --> 00:03:06.130
Yeah.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.890
The thing Barack was finishing his book

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.460
as it was just announced

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.560
that his books are going to be
published after the election.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.030
So he actually spent most
of the summer locked away

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.920
writing the book.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.690
So he's had limited time
to get on my nerves,

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.060
but then he sort of
has gotten on my nerves

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.310
because I haven't seen him enough.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.702
He can't win.

00:03:29.702 --> 00:03:31.182
He can't win, he can't win.

00:03:31.182 --> 00:03:32.049
We all know that.

00:03:32.049 --> 00:03:36.743
We know that we can't win and we got it.

00:03:36.743 --> 00:03:39.330
I would think you would
have some sense of,

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:42.340
Hey, excuse me, guy.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.000
I wrote my book a long time ago.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.620
Huge hit, massive, massive hit,

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.030
huge book tour.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.540
What's taking you so long?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.050
Do you ever get to do that to him?

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.783
Well, his book is a little
bigger, a little more,

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.060
little more historical as he would say,

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.540
but yeah, we've managed,

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.210
we're still together

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.751
and he's still alive.

00:04:07.751 --> 00:04:08.584
(laughing)

00:04:08.584 --> 00:04:13.320
That is the perfect sign
that we're making it through

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.110
I think I would have
read about it somewhere

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.392
if you two had split up.

00:04:16.392 --> 00:04:18.642
(laughing)

